  "description": "This Application is to convert an existing roof space (38.01 cubic meters) at 18 Rushden close \nNortholt; into an en-suite  living space (15.6 cubic meters). The proposed development is within an established residential area, the proposal  \nis intended to mirror the already existing terraced building (no.18) and will not distort the aesthetics and character of the street scene but will rather \ncomplement it wholly and completely. The proposed works are confined to the existing dwelling house and its roof structure and do not involve \nany change of use of the land or building. \n\nThe proposal seeks a planning Permission for the proposed development  for the conversion of the existing roof space into \nhabitable accommodation: \n\n1. Comprising of an en-suite bedroom to be used as a home office as well.  \n2. Installation of 2 numbers roof light on the front elevation  not projecting more than 150mm above the existing roof and a full glaze window \n(Juliet balcony) and 1 window on the rear. \n3. Construction of a rear Dormer to provide useful  headroom and useable floor area.\n4. Formation of internal works including new staircase access and all necessary alterations to comply with Building regulations.",
